# Mobile local-first

**`mobile/`** replaces the ~$50/mo AI Studio stack. **Make life easier** — not ads, nags, or guilt. See `mobile/docs/product-ethos.md`.

## Must

- Persist user/history data in **IndexedDB** or **`localStorage`** (`history-store.ts`, sync/retention helpers)
- **UI reads replicas only** — sync from Worker `/v1/*` into IndexedDB (`sync.ts`); never write buoy readings to D1 from the browser
- Fetch display fallbacks from the **client** where allowed (`buoy-api.ts`: Worker/IDB first; Capacitor may call King County directly)
- Local Vite `/api/kc` proxy is **dev-only** — not available on GitHub Pages
- Add **Settings copy** for any new background fetch (local-only, frequency, cost)
- Add **tests** for new persistence or collection rules (`mobile-tests` / `tests.mdc`)

## Must not (in `mobile/`)

- Firebase, Firestore, Express, Cloud Run, developer REST API, server-side history (free tier)
- **Ads** — no ad SDKs; never gate features behind ads or rewarded video
- **Donation nags** — donate lives in Settings only; no popups or interstitials
- API keys or cloud sync without explicit user request and tradeoff discussion
- Port patterns from the archived AI Studio root (`server.ts`, developer API)
- Reintroduce Cloudflare Pages Functions (`functions/api/kc.ts`) for the web PWA

## Policy

**$0 hosting, no ads:** [mobile/docs/zero-cost-policy.md](mobile/docs/zero-cost-policy.md). Optional paid cloud backup is not required for sustainability.

Full checklist and review workflow: **`mobile-local-first`** skill (`mobile/.cursor/skills/mobile-local-first/SKILL.md`).
